        "content": "To analyze **8.7 Network-Layer Security (IPsec & VPNs): AH vs. ESP Tunnel Mode, Security Associations & IKE** quantitatively, computer networking relies on precise mathematical models, bit-level header specifications, and deterministic state-update equations. The Governing Equation and Architectural Reference Table below summarize the core relationships for **Chapter 8 (Network Security (Symmetric/Public-Key Crypto, Signatures/PKI, TLS 1.3, IPsec, WPA2/5G & Firewalls))**:\n\n$$\\text{RSA: } c = m^e \\bmod n, \\quad m = c^d \\bmod n \\quad (e \\cdot d \\equiv 1 \\bmod (p-1)(q-1)), \\qquad \\text{Cert}_B = K_{\\text{CA}}^-\\big(\\text{Bob},\\, K_B^+\\big)$$\n\n| Security Layer & Protocol | Cryptographic Construction | Security Guarantees (Confidentiality, Integrity, Auth) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Symmetric Crypto (AES)** | 128/192/256-bit Substitution-Permutation Network (`CBC` / `GCM`) | High-speed bulk data encryption using shared secret key $K_S$; requires unique IV/nonce per packet to prevent replay |\n| **Public-Key & Hybrid Crypto** | RSA ($n=pq$) and Ephemeral Diffie-Hellman (`ECDHE`) | Establishes shared session keys over insecure channels with Forward Secrecy; avoids slow public-key encryption on bulk payloads |\n| **MACs, Signatures & PKI** | $\\text{HMAC}(K, m)$, Digital Signature $K_B^-(H(m))$, X.509 CAs | Cryptographic hashes (`SHA-256`) + private-key signatures bind public keys to verified identities via Certification Authorities |\n| **TLS 1.3 (RFC 8446)** | 1-RTT Handshake (`ClientHello` + `KeyShare` $\\to$ `ServerHello` + `Cert`) | Secures HTTP/HTTPS and application streams at L4/L5 using mandatory `ECDHE` forward secrecy and AEAD (`AES-GCM`) |\n| **IPsec ESP (VPNs)** | Tunnel vs. Transport Mode; Security Associations (`SPI`, `SeqNum`) | Encrypts and authenticates complete IP datagrams between enterprise gateways or remote hosts at Layer 3 |\n| **WPA2/5G Auth & Firewalls** | EAPOL 4-Way Handshake (`PMK` $\\to$ `PTK`), 5G `SUCI`/`AUSF`, Stateful ACLs | Mutual wireless authentication without exposing long-term keys (`IMSI`/`SUPI`); perimeter packet filtering and IDS/IPS (`Snort`) |"
